{{also|Proletariat|prolétariat|proletariát}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[proletariate]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|prolétariat||lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|proletarius||lang=la|a man whose only wealth is his offspring, or whose sole service to the state is as father}}, from {{term|proles||lang=la|offspring, posterity}}

===Pronunciation===
{{a|US}} {{enPR|'prōlĭʹtârēət}}, {{IPA|/ˌproʊlɪˈtɛəriət/}}, {{X-SAMPA|%pr\oUlI"tEr\i@t}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|proletariats|-}}

# The [[working class]] or lower [[class]].
#* {{quote-book
|page=173
|year=1906
|author=Karl Marx and Friedrich Engels
|title=Manifesto of the Communist Party
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=s2iEeCJAlusC
|passage="Of all the classes that stand face to face with the bourgeoisie to day the '''proletariat''' alone is a really revolutionary class."}}
# The [[wage earner]]s collectively, excluding [[salaried]] workers.
# {{history}} In ancient Rome, the lowest [[class]] of [[citizen]]s, who had no [[property]].

